WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:10.605
In this video, you will learn every way to share your contest: the link, the QR code, a printable entry poster and yard sign, and an email invitation to your neighbors.

00:00:10.605 --> 00:00:14.168
The more people who know about it, the better the contest.

00:00:14.168 --> 00:00:15.376
We start on the map.

00:00:16.279 --> 00:00:18.028
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:19.812 --> 00:00:22.329
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:24.066 --> 00:00:25.047
Then tap Allow.

00:00:28.181 --> 00:00:30.870
Now look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.065
See the three dots?

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:36.368
That is the menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:36.368 --> 00:00:36.906
Tap them.

00:00:38.526 --> 00:00:40.339
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:42.024 --> 00:00:47.123
That is where every neighborhood contest lives: the ones you can vote in, enter, or run.

00:00:47.824 --> 00:00:48.742
Tap Mine.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.218
This is your personal page.

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:57.402
It lists the contests you run, if you run any, and the homes you entered, with their status.

00:00:58.103 --> 00:01:00.172
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:01:02.552 --> 00:01:05.965
This opens your dashboard, the control room for your contest.

00:01:06.665 --> 00:01:09.860
This is the Overview, the first page of your dashboard.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.200
Scroll down to the card called Share it.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.625
Everything you need to get the word out is in this one card.

00:01:16.525 --> 00:01:18.444
At the top is your contest link.

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:20.770
Tap Copy link, and it is copied for you.

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:27.356
Paste it into an email, a text message, a neighborhood group, or a Facebook post.

00:01:27.356 --> 00:01:33.654
Anyone who opens it lands on your contest page, where they can see the homes, enter their own, and vote.

00:01:34.559 --> 00:01:41.497
Below the link are your two ready-made posters, with your contest name, the dates, and a QR code already on them.

00:01:41.497 --> 00:01:46.548
When someone points their phone camera at the QR code, it opens your contest page.

00:01:46.548 --> 00:01:53.546
That makes them perfect for anything printed, like flyers, signs, and the bulletin board at your local coffee shop.

00:01:54.359 --> 00:01:59.073
Tap Print entry poster for the one made for a bulletin board or a shop window.

00:01:59.073 --> 00:02:00.147
Here is a sample.

00:02:00.147 --> 00:02:08.798
It is festive, so it gets noticed, and it shows your contest name, a big QR code, the deadline to enter, and the words, scan to enter your home.

00:02:08.798 --> 00:02:11.065
Its job is to get neighbors to enter.

00:02:11.065 --> 00:02:16.077
When you print, turn on Background graphics in the print window, so the colors show.

00:02:16.983 --> 00:02:19.615
Print yard sign makes a big sign for a lawn.

00:02:19.615 --> 00:02:20.667
Here is a sample.

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:28.503
It says vote in huge letters, so people can read it from the street, with a QR code that opens the voting page, and the voting dates.

00:02:28.503 --> 00:02:34.818
Put these out when voting opens, and your neighbors can vote while they are standing in front of the lights.

00:02:35.723 --> 00:02:39.436
You can also invite neighbors by email, right from the dashboard.

00:02:39.436 --> 00:02:42.024
Want to know whether your sharing is working?

00:02:42.024 --> 00:02:42.699
Tap Promote.

00:02:44.422 --> 00:02:46.509
Open Invite neighbors by email.

00:02:46.509 --> 00:02:50.553
Type one address on each line, and add a short personal note.

00:02:50.553 --> 00:02:57.009
A note from a real neighbor gets many more people to open the invitation than a plain message does.

00:02:58.683 --> 00:03:00.747
This is what each neighbor receives.

00:03:00.747 --> 00:03:06.270
It has your contest name, your note, and one clear button that takes them straight to the contest.

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:08.390
They do not need to hunt for anything.

00:03:09.396 --> 00:03:11.850
Next up: Approve and decline entries.
